  "worked_solution": "Since $B$ is invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $0$ can't be an eigenvalue of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =0$ should not be a solution to the corresponding characteristic equation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given equations in turn.\n\n- Equation I could  be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation II could be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation III **cannot** be the characteristic equation of $B$ since $\\lambda =0$ is a root of the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
